{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1500690-thoughts-on-a-rank-challenge","id":1500690,"title":"Thoughts on a rank challenge.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-01-18T19:07:58-08:00","id":1500690,"title":"Thoughts on a rank challenge.","content":"In a LARP running right now a Claith Ragabash is challenging a Fostern Philodox for rank. The Ragabash haven't been playing devil's advocate or question anything the leaders of the sept are doing, however one is going at the Philodox and his brother out of spite and malice. So the Philodox is thinking of accepting the rank challenge and doing in a questions and a scenario if the question is answered to his satisfaction. Want input on if the questions would be appropriate.<br /> <br /> Q) Should a Ragabash or any other Auspice be afraid of fulfilling their duty when it involves someone of higher rank?<br /> <br /> S) How would you as a Ragabash point out the hubris of another of higher rank whose let their pride and self ambition getting in the way of their duty and is harming others?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27523-dkscidmore","name":"Dkscidmore","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-18T22:43:55-08:00","id":1500704,"title":"","content":"Especially in LARP there might be a potential for an unsatisfactory outcome when the challenged garou is do decide on answers/actions that are not clearly a win/loose-choice. So it might be a good idea if the challenged garou is discussing his idea and the things he expects from the challenging garou with the Master of Challenge as a second pair of eyes, so to speak.<br /> <br /> For example, the question could be answered &quot;No&quot;, and that is the honourable answer. But it could also be answered &quot;Depends on many factors, like who the garou of higher rank is and how large the rank gap might be. Fear is ultimately of the wyrm, but having a bad gut feeling about a situation might be insightful, and knowing, that one has to be clever about how and when criticising a higher ranked garou to deliver a lesson instead of just being annoying, are tools of the Ragabash trade.&quot; which would be a wise(er) answer.<br /> <br /> The scenario to be devised is even more subjective to judge. Often a ragabash would play an elaborate trick to showcase how pride and self ambition are getting the way of their duties. But those are often also circumstantial. So, the answer might be something like &quot;If, this or that situation arose, I'd do this and that&quot;. So, the scenario might be difficult to judge, too.<br /> <br /> But in the end, the challenged has to decide yes or no on the new rank. And sure, every other garou could try to prevent the following Rite of Accomplishment to cement the rank increase, but the challenged garou is the first one to decide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}